WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.130
English has several ways to talk
about the past: "I played",

2
00:00:04.180 --> 00:00:06.710
"I was playing", "I used to play".

3
00:00:06.760 --> 00:00:11.010
Pablo tells you about his childhood:
De niño jugaba al fútbol.

4
00:00:11.060 --> 00:00:14.390
That means "As a child
I used to play football.

5
00:00:14.440 --> 00:00:15.390
" But look closely.

6
00:00:15.440 --> 00:00:18.770
There's no extra word
for "used to" anywhere.

7
00:00:18.820 --> 00:00:20.350
So where is it hiding?

8
00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:23.090
In this mission, you'll learn
the pattern of the imperfect

9
00:00:23.140 --> 00:00:24.790
tense for regular verbs.

10
00:00:24.840 --> 00:00:31.210
You'll meet the only three verbs
that break it: ser, ir and ver.

11
00:00:31.260 --> 00:00:33.950
And you'll see the jobs
it does in a story,

12
00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:37.450
from describing a scene to
showing what someone was doing.

13
00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:41.780
Your mission: find where Pablo
hides the words "used to".
